1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,860
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

3
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:11,220
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:19,680
To the left and the right,
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,960
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day.

6
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,220
And the values we had
were about to collapse.

7
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:28,777
Oh, just where do we go next?

8
00:00:28,860 --> 00:00:35,440
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,617
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

10
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,937
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

11
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,217
And listen to your soul.

12
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

13
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

14
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,837
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

15
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,037
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

16
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,900
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

17
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

18
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,777
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

19
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,377
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

20
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

21
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,777
For the future ahead, burning bright.

22
00:01:21,860 --> 00:01:24,197
For what's ahead you see.

23
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:27,640
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,737
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

25
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:34,977
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

26
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,800
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

27
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,097
We'll do it our way the best that we know.

28
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:45,557
With tears and doubts and tone.

29
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,917
We'll go where we all wanna go.

30
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,637
The hate within brings colors of our own.

31
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:53,920
Oh, yeah.

32
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:46,740
King has just been defeated. What?

33
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:50,257
We've defeated the Toby Robo
and the lead performers.

34
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:52,177
This is getting quite

35
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:58,497
serious but

36
00:02:58,580 --> 00:02:59,477
it's not over

37
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:02,657
there are still two
monsters out there who can

38
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,697
stop the Straw Hats it
would take a miracle to

39
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:12,537
defeat but they've come

40
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:15,260
this far the struggle

41
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:19,646
The battle between Luffy and
Kaido grows in intensity, however,

42
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,466
the battle may have an
unexpected consequence.

43
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:26,240
If Kaido is defeated, his
flame clouds will disappear.

44
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:38,620
This will cause Onigashima to crash,

45
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:42,721
and the explosives in its basement
will destroy the entire capital.

46
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:46,497
Then the tens of thousands
of helpless citizens

47
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:49,760
enjoying the Fire Festival
will be incinerated.

48
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,480
You're not touching the flower capital!

49
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,820
Go back where you belong!

50
00:04:06,040 --> 00:04:10,657
To make matters worse, Kanjuro
crafted a massive flame monster.

51
00:04:10,740 --> 00:04:14,237
This manifestation of the Kurozumi
Clan's grudge heads toward

52
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:18,085
the castle basements threatening
to detonate its entire arsenal.

53
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,560
Unless Yamato can stop it.

54
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,780
I knew he'd be here.

55
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:30,666
That fire monster will
show up any second now.

56
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,841
And Roki's blocking the entrance.

57
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:34,997
I don't have time to
get in a fight and grab

58
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,727
the key from him and
pull that massive lever.

59
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:38,710
Fuga!

60
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,460
Can you cover me, Fuga?

61
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:43,730
Fuga!

62
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:47,450
Fuga!

63
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,680
Fuga! Fuga!

64
00:04:57,020 --> 00:04:58,400
Ha-ha! Yay!

65
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:00,480
Thanks a bunch, Fuga!

66
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:02,450
Fuga!

67
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:04,840
You keep Rookie busy for me, okay?

68
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:08,000
Fuga! Rocky!

69
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,230
Hey!

70
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,860
That doesn't look good.

71
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,000
Our bodies back together.

72
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:24,377
I mean, that's a relief, but how
the hell does that even work?

73
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:27,401
We need to get both of you
to chop her right away.

74
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,460
There they are!

75
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:30,797
It's the Straw Hats!

76
00:05:30,880 --> 00:05:31,797
Don't let them escape!

77
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:32,710
Let's go!

78
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:33,860
Take them down!

79
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,997
We got enough problems to deal with!

80
00:05:36,080 --> 00:05:36,910
Go away!

81
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,000
How do you like my skull bomb grass?

82
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,070
Get him!

83
00:05:53,153 --> 00:05:55,037
That guy's got a bounty of 200 million!

84
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,800
Guess this is our lucky day!

85
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,180
I'm so dead! Help!

86
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:02,322
If the bad guys don't get
me, then the fire will!

87
00:06:02,480 --> 00:06:03,940
Just go, Sir Usopp.

88
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:05,258
You must save Kiku.

89
00:06:05,500 --> 00:06:06,520
Leave me behind.

90
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:10,800
No, Master Keen.

91
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,260
I won't make it.

92
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:13,840
Leave me here.

93
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,937
Okay, I'll leave you both and
get out of here on my own!

94
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:19,057
And why did I even bother coming here?!

95
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:21,020
You stupid suicidal samurai!

96
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,137
Chipping with honor is still dying!

97
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:33,157
Don't sacrifice yourself
to take responsibility!

98
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:36,660
I know that's your culture,
but I don't like it one bit!

99
00:06:37,840 --> 00:06:41,134
I'll survive crawling with
snot dripping out of my nose!

100
00:06:41,960 --> 00:06:44,500
If that's what it takes, it's worth it!

101
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:47,490
Usopp!

102
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,856
If I die with dignity, then
who'd be here to help you?

103
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,840
Forgive me, sir Usopp.

104
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:59,057
Just holding on the rain
shouldn't be enough for you!

105
00:06:59,140 --> 00:07:00,500
You have to live!

106
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:04,770
Ah!

107
00:07:04,853 --> 00:07:05,683
Ah!

108
00:07:05,766 --> 00:07:09,335
I did!

109
00:07:09,418 --> 00:07:10,248
Listen to him, you two!

110
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:12,210
Take cover!

111
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:31,217
What the hell is Izo doing here?

112
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:34,020
Did we piss off Whitebeard's
old crew somehow?

113
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:35,960
He's an ex-captain.

114
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,560
And it's not just him.

115
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,857
Marco was here, too.

116
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,234
Why are they after us?

117
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:43,080
Oh, thank you, whoever you are.

118
00:07:43,840 --> 00:07:44,670
Esau.

119
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:55,240
I lost again. I'm sorry.

120
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,220
That's enough.

121
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,877
You'll open your walls.

122
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:03,257
We can catch up as much as we want
later once our country is free.

123
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:05,017
I can't.

124
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:07,640
It's over for me.

125
00:08:08,240 --> 00:08:12,517
As your brother, I won't
allow you to give up.

126
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,017
Understand?

127
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:16,880
Yes.

128
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:22,060
I'll get you out of here
no matter what it takes.

129
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,880
So live.

130
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:28,420
Keep fighting.

131
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:37,917
If you truly believe in straw
hat luffy then you must survive,

132
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,920
right?

133
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,897
Thank you, big brother.

134
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:45,077
You too.

135
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:48,020
Please don't die.

136
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,980
Thank God, Usopp!

137
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:06,370
Yeah?

138
00:09:06,453 --> 00:09:07,792
Wait, you know who I am?

139
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,900
Of course I do!

140
00:09:11,040 --> 00:09:12,393
You're the Sniper King!

141
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:15,860
Take care of those two! You got it!

142
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:24,920
You ready, Hamlet? Of
course! Let's go! And away!

143
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:27,576
It's time to depart on a new journey!

144
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,940
You're dead!

145
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:34,080
No one passes through! Got it?

146
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:55,740
You cut fire first!

147
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:56,940
I've won!

148
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:02,220
Now undo the paralysis, Jutsu! It's over!

149
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,720
Why don't you undo yours first?

150
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,180
I'll be fine!

151
00:10:08,160 --> 00:10:08,990
I see.

152
00:10:09,260 --> 00:10:10,090
You're a fool!

153
00:10:10,173 --> 00:10:11,800
Stubborn to the bitter end!

154
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:15,377
But your Jutsu will be undone
once you burn to death!

155
00:10:15,460 --> 00:10:17,580
I saw the fires Lord Odin faced!

156
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:20,271
This is but a summer breeze in comparison!

157
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:29,840
I feel like I'm in a dream.

158
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:34,517
Komurasaki is alive and the fools
on this island will soon be dead.

159
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,720
It's literally music to my ears.

160
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:39,314
What's taking you so long, Fukurokuju?

161
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,716
We need to get out of here
before this place explodes.

162
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:46,660
My lord, is anything the matter?

163
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,440
Oh no, just thinking.

164
00:10:49,940 --> 00:10:53,200
Say, while we're here, why
not play that song for me?

165
00:10:53,860 --> 00:10:54,860
You know the one.

166
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:55,980
It's my favorite.

167
00:10:56,220 --> 00:10:57,677
I haven't heard it in ages.

168
00:10:57,760 --> 00:10:59,120
Yes, of course

169
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,580
They got drake.

170
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:17,780
let's fuck it in b!

171
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:23,140
We got no reason to fight those guys!

172
00:11:25,900 --> 00:11:27,180
Sorry, Snake.

173
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,820
Tough luck, Drake.

174
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:39,220
That was a nuisance and
a waste of our time.

175
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,935
They're quite strong.

176
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,440
Seems Apu ran away.

177
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:50,280
Do you have Nico Robin in custody yet?

178
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:51,420
It's in progress.

179
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:52,696
We were interrupted.

180
00:11:52,820 --> 00:11:53,760
Well, hurry up.

181
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,777
We need to get out of this castle.

182
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:58,095
All the lead performers were defeated.

183
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,430
Impossible!

184
00:12:05,420 --> 00:12:08,237
The worst generation is still
fighting an uphill battle,

185
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:10,438
but if they manage to pull this off,

186
00:12:11,100 --> 00:12:13,100
it'll be quite the story indeed.

187
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:22,517
There will be a massive upset
in the balance of power,

188
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:24,097
one that would fan the flames of every

189
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:26,886
little fire we're trying
to put out right now.

190
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:32,291
What happens at the end of this battle
will set the course for our next age.

191
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:34,534
That's certainly true.

192
00:12:36,680 --> 00:12:37,840
But what then?

193
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:43,760
Is mankind even capable of more than this?

194
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:05,200
All right, go, go, go!

195
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,200
Try that again!

196
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:46,200
No! No! No! No!

197
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:00,310
Kosarki!

198
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,920
Now, GumGum!

199
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:24,457
If I hear GumGum one more time...

200
00:14:24,540 --> 00:14:26,280
Better get used to it!

201
00:14:27,040 --> 00:14:27,960
Rockside!

202
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:11,360
I'm starting to have some fun.

203
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,660
Ah, so am I.

204
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,860
One more round!

205
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,984
Haven't you had enough already?

206
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:34,140
Take it easy!

207
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:35,840
U .A .R.

208
00:15:36,140 --> 00:15:37,964
We get to drink one day a year!

209
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,417
I'm gonna catch it up today!

210
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:41,177
Just let me have my fun.

211
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:43,580
It's back to suffering after this.

212
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,480
Screw you, Arachis!

213
00:15:46,920 --> 00:15:48,240
Will you cut it out?

214
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:52,517
Public officials could
be watching us right now!

215
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,430
Hey, look.

216
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:56,140
They're setting up the skyships.

217
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,860
The festival's about to wrap up.

218
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:04,330
Wow!

219
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:07,500
Look at all the lanterns!

220
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,678
Write down a wish to your ancestors.

221
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:21,687
They'll see it up in heaven.

222
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,240
I know just what to wish for!

223
00:16:25,640 --> 00:16:26,470
Here.

224
00:16:26,553 --> 00:16:27,480
Go ahead and write one.

225
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:29,840
It'll come true?

226
00:16:30,140 --> 00:16:31,540
It's really that easy?

227
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:35,195
You know why they call them sky ships?

228
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:40,440
Because they go all the way to heaven beyond
the sky, where our lost loved ones are.

229
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:45,360
You really think Daddy's
gonna read my wish?

230
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:48,040
Yes, he'll be happy to see it.

231
00:17:01,640 --> 00:17:03,997
Hey, why are you boozing it up right now?

232
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:04,962
We're fighting!

233
00:17:07,040 --> 00:17:09,260
Cause I'm having a good time.

234
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,957
Everyone is drinking.

235
00:17:12,040 --> 00:17:14,337
It's the fire festival in the capital.

236
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:19,577
We were supposed to have a party on
Onigashima too until you screwed that up.

237
00:17:19,660 --> 00:17:21,797
Now do you want some or what?

238
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,597
You don't have a care in the world.

239
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:26,617
Do you tell me you're drunk already?

240
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:30,137
This is just a little sip.

241
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:32,160
I ain't drunk.

242
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,780
Why are you so mean to me?

243
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:41,600
I worked so hard on this
party and you ruined it!

244
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:55,540
I knew it!

245
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:57,057
You're drunk off your ass!

246
00:17:57,140 --> 00:17:59,493
What's wrong with letting loose a bitch?

247
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:02,420
Now, watch!

248
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:08,120
Oops! Come on!

249
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,555
You can't even stand!

250
00:18:13,380 --> 00:18:16,200
How are you supposed
to fight me like that?!

251
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:18,317
I kick your ass!

252
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:20,576
You better not use this as an excuse!

253
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:27,160
You're so funny!

254
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:35,480
I'll make myself weak
and all. Take a hint.

255
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:38,780
I'm showing you that I accept you.

256
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:40,930
Uh...

257
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:42,100
Gum-Gum!

258
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:54,720
Drunken Dragon Blah Blah!

259
00:18:58,460 --> 00:19:00,680
I'm really feeling it now.

260
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:03,640
I acknowledge your strength, Strahd.

261
00:19:03,980 --> 00:19:08,686
You're the first person who's been able
to go toe-to-toe with me in a long time.

262
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:22,920
Wiping hammer!

263
00:19:25,680 --> 00:19:27,380
What do I do?

264
00:20:01,460 --> 00:20:07,897
Look at this place what
a mess everything's

265
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,397
ruined I've been having fun going

266
00:20:10,480 --> 00:20:13,957
wild but Now my castle's all screwed up

267
00:20:14,040 --> 00:20:20,000
look at me I can't even save my own home

268
00:20:20,740 --> 00:20:22,840
